collections:
  - folderType: environment
    name: Swagger Petstore
    documentation: |-
      # Swagger Petstore

      This is a sample server Petstore server.  You can find out more about Swagger at [http://swagger.io](http://swagger.io) or on [irc.freenode.net, #swagger](http://swagger.io/irc/).  For this sample, you can use the api key &#x60;special-key&#x60; to test the authorization filters.

      **Version:** 1.0.7

      **Terms of Service:** [http://swagger.io/terms/](http://swagger.io/terms/)

      ## Contact

      - **Email:** [apiteam@swagger.io](mailto:apiteam@swagger.io)

      ## License

      [Apache 2.0](http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.html)

      ## External Documentation

      [Find out more about Swagger](http://swagger.io)

      **Host:** `localhost:8080`

      **Base Path:** `/api`

      **Schemes:** `https`, `http`

      ## Models

      ```mermaid
      classDiagram
        class Category {
          - id? : integer
          - name? : string
        }
        class Pet {
          - id? : integer
          - category? : Category
          + name : string
          + photoUrls : array<string>
          - tags? : array<Tag>
          - status? : string
        }
        class Tag {
          - id? : integer
          - name? : string
        }
        class ApiResponse {
          - code? : integer
          - type? : string
          - message? : string
        }
        class Order {
          - id? : integer
          - petId? : integer
          - quantity? : integer
          - shipDate? : string
          - status? : string
          - complete? : boolean
        }
        class User {
          - id? : integer
          - username? : string
          - firstName? : string
          - lastName? : string
          - email? : string
          - password? : string
          - phone? : string
          - userStatus? : integer
        }
        Pet --> Category
        Pet --> Tag
      ```
    tags: []
    configuration: {}
    environments:
      - name: Default
        variables:
          - key: port
            value:
              type: numeric
              value: 8080
              format: decimal
            description: ''
            enabled: true
          - key: scheme
            value:
              type: string
              value: http
            description: ''
            enabled: true
          - key: domain
            value:
              type: string
              value: localhost
            description: ''
            enabled: true
          - key: baseUrl
            value:
              type: string
              value: '{{scheme}}://{{domain}}:{{port}}'
            description: ''
            enabled: true
          - key: test
            value:
              type: password
            description: ''
            enabled: true
          - key: col
            value:
              type: color
              value: '#d81111'
            description: ''
            enabled: true
          - key: dt
            value:
              type: datetime
              value: '2026-01-23T01:47:42.000Z'
              format: yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss
            description: ''
            enabled: true
        subEnvironments:
          - name: Production
            variables:
              - key: scheme
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: https
                description: ''
              - key: domain
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: petstore.com
                description: ''
              - key: baseUrl
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: '{{scheme}}://{{domain}}:{{port}}'
                description: ''
    items:
      - name: pet
        documentation: "# pet\r\n\r\nEverything about your Pets\r\n\r\n## External Documentation\r\n\r\n[Find out more](http://swagger.io)"
        tags:
          - pet
        configuration: {}
        items:
          - type: http
            name: Find pet by ID
            documentation: |-
              # Find pet by ID

              Returns a single pet

              **Operation ID:** `getPetById`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `petId` | path | integer (int64) | Yes | ID of pet to return |

              ## Types

              ### Pet

              **Reference:** `#/definitions/Pet`

              ```mermaid
              classDiagram
                class Pet {
                  - id? : integer
                  - category? : Category
                  + name : string
                  + photoUrls : array<string>
                  - tags? : array<Tag>
                  - status? : string
                }
              ```


              | Property | Type | Required | Description |
              |----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `id` | integer | No |  |
              | `category` | Category | No |  |
              | `name` | string | Yes |  |
              | `photoUrls` | array&lt;string&gt; | Yes |  |
              | `tags` | array&lt;Tag&gt; | No |  |
              | `status` | string | No | pet status in the store |


              ## Responses

              ### 200
              successful operation

              **Schema:** `#/definitions/Pet`


              ### 400
              Invalid ID supplied



              ### 404
              Pet not found



              ## Security

              - **api_key**
            tags:
              - pet
            method: GET
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet/{{petId}}'
            headers: []
            params: []
            pathParams:
              - key: petId
                value:
                  type: numeric
                  value: 20
                  format: decimal
                description: ID of pet to return
                enabled: true
            notes: ''
            body:
              type: text
              content: ''
          - type: http
            name: Updates a pet in the store with form data
            documentation: |-
              # Updates a pet in the store with form data

              **Operation ID:** `updatePetWithForm`

              ## Consumes

              - `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `petId` | path | integer (int64) | Yes | ID of pet that needs to be updated |
              | `name` | formData | string | No | Updated name of the pet |
              | `status` | formData | string | No | Updated status of the pet |

              ## Responses

              ### 405
              Invalid input



              ## Security

              - **petstore_auth**: `write:pets`, `read:pets`
            tags:
              - pet
            method: POST
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet/{{petId}}'
            headers: []
            params: []
            pathParams:
              - key: petId
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: ''
                description: ID of pet that needs to be updated
                enabled: true
            body:
              type: x-www-form-urlencoded
              fields:
                - key: name
                  value:
                    type: string
                    value: ''
                  description: Updated name of the pet
                  enabled: true
                - key: status
                  value:
                    type: string
                    value: ''
                  description: Updated status of the pet
                  enabled: true
          - type: http
            name: Deletes a pet
            documentation: |-
              # Deletes a pet

              **Operation ID:** `deletePet`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `api_key` | header | string | No |  |
              | `petId` | path | integer (int64) | Yes | Pet id to delete |

              ## Responses

              ### 400
              Invalid ID supplied



              ### 404
              Pet not found



              ## Security

              - **petstore_auth**: `write:pets`, `read:pets`
            tags:
              - pet
            method: DELETE
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet/{{petId}}'
            headers:
              - key: api_key
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: ''
                description: ''
                enabled: true
            params: []
            pathParams:
              - key: petId
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: ''
                description: Pet id to delete
                enabled: true
            body:
              type: text
              content: ''
          - type: http
            name: uploads an image
            documentation: |-
              # uploads an image

              **Operation ID:** `uploadFile`

              ## Consumes

              - `multipart/form-data`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `petId` | path | integer (int64) | Yes | ID of pet to update |
              | `additionalMetadata` | formData | string | No | Additional data to pass to server |
              | `file` | formData | file | No | file to upload |

              ## Types

              ### ApiResponse

              **Reference:** `#/definitions/ApiResponse`

              ```mermaid
              classDiagram
                class ApiResponse {
                  - code? : integer
                  - type? : string
                  - message? : string
                }
              ```


              | Property | Type | Required | Description |
              |----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `code` | integer | No |  |
              | `type` | string | No |  |
              | `message` | string | No |  |


              ## Responses

              ### 200
              successful operation

              **Schema:** `#/definitions/ApiResponse`


              ## Security

              - **petstore_auth**: `write:pets`, `read:pets`
            tags:
              - pet
            method: POST
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet/{{petId}}/uploadImage'
            headers: []
            params: []
            pathParams:
              - key: petId
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: ''
                description: ID of pet to update
            body:
              type: form-data
              fields:
                - key: additionalMetadata
                  value:
                    type: string
                    value: ''
                  description: Additional data to pass to server
                  enabled: true
                - key: file
                  value:
                    type: string
                    value: ''
                  description: file to upload
                  enabled: true
          - type: http
            name: Add a new pet to the store
            documentation: |-
              # Add a new pet to the store

              **Operation ID:** `addPet`

              ## Consumes

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `body` | body | #/definitions/Pet | Yes | Pet object that needs to be added to the store |

              ## Types

              ### Pet

              **Reference:** `#/definitions/Pet`

              ```mermaid
              classDiagram
                class Pet {
                  - id? : integer
                  - category? : Category
                  + name : string
                  + photoUrls : array<string>
                  - tags? : array<Tag>
                  - status? : string
                }
              ```


              | Property | Type | Required | Description |
              |----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `id` | integer | No |  |
              | `category` | Category | No |  |
              | `name` | string | Yes |  |
              | `photoUrls` | array&lt;string&gt; | Yes |  |
              | `tags` | array&lt;Tag&gt; | No |  |
              | `status` | string | No | pet status in the store |


              ## Responses

              ### 405
              Invalid input



              ## Security

              - **petstore_auth**: `write:pets`, `read:pets`
            tags:
              - pet
            method: POST
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet'
            headers:
              - key: Content-Type
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: application/json
                description: ''
                enabled: true
            params:
              - key: ''
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: ''
                description: ''
                enabled: true
            pathParams: []
            body:
              type: text
              content: |-
                {
                  "id": 20,
                  "category": {
                    "id": 3,
                    "name": "string"
                  },
                  "name": "test111",
                  "photoUrls": [
                  ],
                  "tags": [],
                  "status": "available"
                }
          - type: http
            name: Update an existing pet
            documentation: |-
              # Update an existing pet

              **Operation ID:** `updatePet`

              ## Consumes

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `body` | body | #/definitions/Pet | Yes | Pet object that needs to be added to the store |

              ## Types

              ### Pet

              **Reference:** `#/definitions/Pet`

              ```mermaid
              classDiagram
                class Pet {
                  - id? : integer
                  - category? : Category
                  + name : string
                  + photoUrls : array<string>
                  - tags? : array<Tag>
                  - status? : string
                }
              ```


              | Property | Type | Required | Description |
              |----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `id` | integer | No |  |
              | `category` | Category | No |  |
              | `name` | string | Yes |  |
              | `photoUrls` | array&lt;string&gt; | Yes |  |
              | `tags` | array&lt;Tag&gt; | No |  |
              | `status` | string | No | pet status in the store |


              ## Responses

              ### 400
              Invalid ID supplied



              ### 404
              Pet not found



              ### 405
              Validation exception



              ## Security

              - **petstore_auth**: `write:pets`, `read:pets`
            tags:
              - pet
            method: PUT
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet'
            headers: []
            params: []
            pathParams: []
            body:
              type: text
              content: |-
                {
                  "id": 0,
                  "category": {
                    "id": 0,
                    "name": ""
                  },
                  "name": "",
                  "photoUrls": [
                    ""
                  ],
                  "tags": [
                    {
                      "id": 0,
                      "name": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "status": "available"
                }
          - type: http
            name: Finds Pets by status
            documentation: |-
              # Finds Pets by status

              Multiple status values can be provided with comma separated strings

              **Operation ID:** `findPetsByStatus`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `status` | query | array | Yes | Status values that need to be considered for filter |

              ## Responses

              ### 200
              successful operation

              **Schema:** `array`


              ### 400
              Invalid status value



              ## Security

              - **petstore_auth**: `write:pets`, `read:pets`
            tags:
              - pet
            method: GET
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet/findByStatus'
            headers: []
            params:
              - key: status
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: ''
                description: Status values that need to be considered for filter
                enabled: true
            pathParams: []
            notes: ''
          - type: http
            name: Finds Pets by tags
            documentation: |-
              # Finds Pets by tags

              Multiple tags can be provided with comma separated strings. Use tag1, tag2, tag3 for testing.

              **Operation ID:** `findPetsByTags`

              > ⚠️ **Deprecated:** This endpoint is deprecated and may be removed in future versions.

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `tags` | query | array | Yes | Tags to filter by |

              ## Responses

              ### 200
              successful operation

              **Schema:** `array`


              ### 400
              Invalid tag value



              ## Security

              - **petstore_auth**: `write:pets`, `read:pets`
            tags:
              - pet
            method: GET
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet/findByTags'
            headers: []
            params:
              - key: tags
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: ''
                description: Tags to filter by
            pathParams: []
            deprecated: true
      - name: store
        documentation: "# store\r\n\r\nAccess to Petstore orders"
        tags:
          - store
        configuration: {}
        items:
          - type: http
            name: Returns pet inventories by status
            documentation: |-
              # Returns pet inventories by status

              Returns a map of status codes to quantities

              **Operation ID:** `getInventory`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`

              ## Responses

              ### 200
              successful operation

              **Schema:** `object`


              ## Security

              - **api_key**
            tags:
              - store
            method: GET
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/store/inventory'
            headers: []
            params: []
            pathParams: []
          - type: http
            name: Find purchase order by ID
            documentation: |-
              # Find purchase order by ID

              For valid response try integer IDs with value &gt;&#x3D; 1 and &lt;&#x3D; 10. Other values will generated exceptions

              **Operation ID:** `getOrderById`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `orderId` | path | integer (int64) | Yes | ID of pet that needs to be fetched |

              ## Types

              ### Order

              **Reference:** `#/definitions/Order`

              ```mermaid
              classDiagram
                class Order {
                  - id? : integer
                  - petId? : integer
                  - quantity? : integer
                  - shipDate? : string
                  - status? : string
                  - complete? : boolean
                }
              ```


              | Property | Type | Required | Description |
              |----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `id` | integer | No |  |
              | `petId` | integer | No |  |
              | `quantity` | integer | No |  |
              | `shipDate` | string | No |  |
              | `status` | string | No | Order Status |
              | `complete` | boolean | No |  |


              ## Responses

              ### 200
              successful operation

              **Schema:** `#/definitions/Order`


              ### 400
              Invalid ID supplied



              ### 404
              Order not found
            tags:
              - store
            method: GET
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/store/order/{{orderId}}'
            headers: []
            params: []
            pathParams:
              - key: orderId
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: ''
                description: ID of pet that needs to be fetched
          - type: http
            name: Delete purchase order by ID
            documentation: |-
              # Delete purchase order by ID

              For valid response try integer IDs with positive integer value. Negative or non-integer values will generate API errors

              **Operation ID:** `deleteOrder`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `orderId` | path | integer (int64) | Yes | ID of the order that needs to be deleted |

              ## Responses

              ### 400
              Invalid ID supplied



              ### 404
              Order not found
            tags:
              - store
            method: DELETE
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/store/order/{{orderId}}'
            headers: []
            params: []
            pathParams:
              - key: orderId
                value:
                  type: string
                  value: ''
                description: ID of the order that needs to be deleted
          - type: http
            name: Place an order for a pet
            documentation: |-
              # Place an order for a pet

              **Operation ID:** `placeOrder`

              ## Consumes

              - `application/json`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `body` | body | #/definitions/Order | Yes | order placed for purchasing the pet |

              ## Types

              ### Order

              **Reference:** `#/definitions/Order`

              ```mermaid
              classDiagram
                class Order {
                  - id? : integer
                  - petId? : integer
                  - quantity? : integer
                  - shipDate? : string
                  - status? : string
                  - complete? : boolean
                }
              ```


              | Property | Type | Required | Description |
              |----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `id` | integer | No |  |
              | `petId` | integer | No |  |
              | `quantity` | integer | No |  |
              | `shipDate` | string | No |  |
              | `status` | string | No | Order Status |
              | `complete` | boolean | No |  |


              ## Responses

              ### 200
              successful operation

              **Schema:** `#/definitions/Order`


              ### 400
              Invalid Order
            tags:
              - store
            method: POST
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/store/order'
            headers: []
            params: []
            pathParams: []
            body:
              type: text
              content: |-
                {
                  "id": 0,
                  "petId": 0,
                  "quantity": 0,
                  "shipDate": "",
                  "status": "placed",
                  "complete": false
                }
      - name: user
        documentation: "# user\r\n\r\nOperations about user\r\n\r\n## External Documentation\r\n\r\n[Find out more about our store](http://swagger.io)"
        tags:
          - user
        configuration: {}
        items:
          - type: http
            name: Creates list of users with given input array
            documentation: |-
              # Creates list of users with given input array

              **Operation ID:** `createUsersWithListInput`

